ring the  doors but among the people that do  answer sometimes there's interest  sometimes people just want you to leave  sometimes you can kind of glean that  these people are Trump supporters or  maybe they're going for another  candidate but you get all sorts of  strange responses honestly I wonder too  if it's if it's the best campaigning  strategy but I think just even being out  there even you know having people drive  by other roads or any supporters walking  by trying to canvass I think even that  stuff helps with voter turnout so that's  why in the end I was glad I did it do  they give you Bernie paraphernalia so  that you're visually identified as a  Bernie supporter yeah we had stickers we  had literature in our hands so for the  people who didn't answer their doors  they got some literature so you know  that was that was great  but it didn't it didn't honestly seem  all that well here's the thing so I  assumed that we would be assigned a  neighborhood and you know maybe have  like three or four streets and we'd have  yeah right every single house on that  street yeah that we'd have to eat every  single house on that street because you  know every voters important in New  Hampshire they have same-day voter  registrations so why not just go to  every single house and talk to as many  people as you possibly can but they only  wanted us to go to specific houses and  we were using an app for it and maybe we  would go to like one big street and  there would only be three doors that  we'd have to knock on and so you know I  don't know the internals of all this  maybe this is the best campaigning  strategy but to me it seemed as if maybe  it would have been more effective just  to try to reach out to everyone and then  you know sort of log our results from  that the responses that we got from that  but I wonder if the idea is to target  known voters and known Democratic voters  or like yeah I'm curious what the  strategy is and we also noticed that  some of the houses that we went to we  already saw Bernie paraphernalia there  or in one case someone had said like all  the Bernie people already came by twice  so you know I I hope it's not just that  they're having sort of problems with the  operation at large but I think a big  part of the reason why there was there  was so much chaos was that there were  just so many volunteers which is  actually like a blessing in disguise  that's a good problem to have right and  so at first we were only assigned like  2025 doors that was actually we were  first assigned to an apartment complex  which was tough because you have to be  buzzed in or like wait for someone to  come out and you know people aren't  necessarily willing to buzz you in if  they know you're working for a campaign  like they don't want to talk to you in  the first place so that was tricky but  then later we were in like a more of a  suburban area and that was a little bit  more enjoyable got to you know have a  little bit of exercise walking around  the streets of New Hampshire at the very  least and so the transportation just  gets you to Nashua and then you're on  foot the rest of the way no we actually  had a carpool there's a carpool so one  of the other canvassers was driving us  around and dropping off us off in  different locations from that  perspective it was actually organized  very very well and we stopped for lunch  at one point at this nice New Hampshire  cafe I forget the name of it and we saw  we saw a cameraman  off in the corner of the cafe and we  were like oh what is this for he goes oh  it's for PBS there  very cool we start to finish up our  lunch and like clean up the table so  that more people can come in and you  know sit at the table and as I'm getting  up to leave I look over and judy  woodruff s'right there and she asked me  if we're done eating there and I'm like  yes yes we are and I didn't notice  they're quite at that point but later  max told me who it was and I was very  starstruck so she was just looking for a  table to have a sandwich basically  basically yeah it was it was a big  moment in my life I mean tim robbins and  judy woodruff in the same day it was a  starstruck day yeah yeah so definitely  just on that alone definitely worth  going up there I think did you find that  the cafe had plenty of vegan options  plenty of vegan options I was blown away  well I thought yeah yeah I was  definitely blown away and you know maybe  because maybe I just want to I should  probably bring this up to you  I think we had one good story from from  this canvas thing that made it all  worthwhile which was that we went to one  apartment and we ran into a Bernie  supporter who said that he thought it  was too late like he didn't realize that  New Hampshire had same-day registration  and so he thought it was all over he was  a Bernie fan but he didn't think he  would be able to vote and you know just  us showing up there and delivering that  news to him I think we got out the vote  that way so you know I don't know how  many total people we convinced her  brought to our side I don't know if it  was even five people but you know we did  our part we tried at least well listen  if Bernie wins by one you and Max will  single-handedly be responsible for  turning the New Hampshire primary over  to Bernie Sanders which so let's keep  that in our back pocket as we watch the  results come in tomorrow night I hope  you will join me for a results live  stream tomorrow Tuesday night with the  New Hampshire primary results I had been  invited by a group of journalists to go  up to New Hampshire the way we did back  in 2016 and interview voters and there's  a they've rented out like an entire bar  and it's a good setup but I know that I  would not be able to do as good of a  show I wouldn't be able to do audience  participation it would be a mess half  the time the Internet at these things is  very very spotty so I decided I'm gonna  stay stateside literally in the state of  Massachusetts and/or Commonwealth and I  am going to be doing the results live  show on YouTube  which and Facebook live so that'll be  tomorrow night but we've got tomorrow's  show and bonus show coming up long  before that the david pakman show at  david pakman.com  [Music]
 

